348	    <p class="callout"><strong>Disabled state.</strong> Use <code>--arxiv-grey-dis</code> (<code>#b0aba6</code>)
349	    for the disabled color and set <code>pointer-events: none</code>. The underline stays so it's still
350	    recognisable as a (currently-unavailable) link. The disabled state falls below AA on contrast — WCAG
351	    exempts disabled controls from contrast requirements.</p>
352	
353	    <p class="callout"><strong>Visited memory.</strong> The Visited Purple is intentionally strong, not
354	    a faint after-state. Researchers reading long bibliographies and listings benefit from seeing what
355	    they've already followed up on; a too-subtle visited treatment defeats the purpose. If a specific
356	    surface (e.g., a navigation breadcrumb) needs to suppress visited styling, override
357	    <code>:visited { color: inherit }</code> locally.</p>
