363	  <section class="section">
364	    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
365	    <p class="section-desc">Two patterns for applying the styles.</p>
366	
367	    <p class="callout"><strong>Utility class.</strong> Add <code>.ds-link</code> to specific anchors
368	    you want to style. Use this when you're cherry-picking — for example, in a page where some links
369	    should follow the public-side treatment and others (button-styled, nav-styled) should not.</p>
370	    <pre style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e0dbd7; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--arxiv-font-mono); font-size: 12px; overflow-x: auto;"><code style="background: none; padding: 0;">&lt;a class="ds-link" href="..."&gt;link text&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>
371	
372	    <p class="callout"><strong>Scoped base rule.</strong> Apply the same styling to every <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>
373	    inside a content surface (article, paragraph block) without per-anchor classes.</p>
374	    <pre style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e0dbd7; padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--arxiv-font-mono); font-size: 12px; overflow-x: auto;"><code style="background: none; padding: 0;">.article-body a {
375	  color: var(--arxiv-link-blue);
376	  text-decoration: underline;
377	  text-underline-offset: 2px;
378	}
379	.article-body a:hover    { color: var(--arxiv-link-hover); }
380	.article-body a:visited  { color: var(--arxiv-link-visited); }
381	.article-body a:focus-visible {
382	  outline: 3px solid var(--arxiv-focus-ring);
383	  outline-offset: 2px;
384	}</code></pre>
385	  </section>
